packet={'schema_version':1,'artifact_kind':'independent-primary-first-source-API-prerequisite','status':'CLOSED_TYPED_OBLIGATION_REFINEMENT','reviewer_id':V,'observed_HEAD':subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],text=True).strip(),'synthesis_first':{'finding':'The required compact-C2 entropy/mass/derivative-square convergence needs no new CLT or unbounded-integral theorem. Actual35 output plus three true BCFs and integral-map domain transfer suffices. Use root ofCompactSupport to avoid porting SLT bespoke boundedness/BCF constructors. Zero entropy mass is admitted through continuous tlogt.','smallest_next_target':'One genuine actual count-law integration node producing three observer L1 domains on gaussianReal0,1 and every actual finite count law, three observer integral limits and their actual entropy limit, with only f: R->R, ContDiff R 2 f and HasCompactSupport f as public analytic binders. Obtain actual law sequence by calling35 internally; no supplied law/limit/normalizer/L1/entropy certificate.','dependency_ready_condition':'35 publicly sealed interface is sufficient, but its exact admitted compiled state is deliberately not certified or inferred by this preread. Mathematical implementation of36 waits35 independent admission.'},'primary_first':{'source':prior['primary_source']['raw'],'outer_fragments':fragments,'contract':'SPHMC S4.E6 first inequality uses full standard-Gaussian LSI AND separate Gaussian Talagrand. It does not print this finite Bernoulli/CLT proof, impose compact support on literal RGO square-root density, or give either dependency for free. This packet is authored compact analytic core only.'},'fixed_definitions':{'cube':'B_N = Fin N -> Bool, actual canonical measurable finite cube.','mu_N':'(Fintype.card B_N : ENNReal)^(-1) smul Measure.count; cardinal=2^N>0. Fin0 cube has cardinal1.','S_N':'(sqrt(N:Real))^(-1) * sum_i (if eps_i then1 else-1). Exactly same35 output map, no change to +/- convention or scaling. At N0 sum0 and totalized inverse0 give S0=0.','gamma':'gaussianReal0 (1:NNReal), exact covariance/variance1.','observables':{'A_f':'x -> (f x)^2','B_f':'x -> (f x)^2 * Real.log((f x)^2)','C_f':'x -> (deriv f x)^2'},'entropy':'Ent_m(f^2) = integral B_f dm - (integral A_f dm)*Real.log(integral A_f dm). No integrability is implicit in totalized integral notation; derive and output the real L1 domains.'},'public35_signature_only':{'file':sigpath.as_posix(),'raw_sha256':desc(sigpath)['raw_sha256'],'signature_text':seal['signature_text'],'read_scope':'Only preproof statement/signature, not production body, blind output, wholemath or source verdict.'},'upstream_source':{'revision':'SLT d0f506f0a695018265dccb33bcb05e2f5ca1c876','license':'Apache2 headers in all inspected snapshots; external static references, not compiled local truth.','predicate_expansion':'EfronSteinApp.CompactlySupportedSmooth f = ContDiff R 2 f AND HasCompactSupport f; not C-infinity.','actual_parents':['GaussianPoincare.tendsto_integral_f_sq','GaussianPoincare.tendsto_integral_deriv_sq','GaussianPoincare.tendsto_integral_f_sq_mul_log','GaussianPoincare.tendsto_entropy_f_sq','GaussianLSI.gaussian_logSobolev_CompSmo'], 'entropy_definition':'LogSobolev.entropy exactly same homogeneous real entropy integral, no probability normalization smuggled into f.','split':'OneDimGLSICompSmo combines entropy limit and SEPARATE tendsto_sum_sq_shifted_four_deriv_sq. Derivative-square expectation convergence alone is not factor4 full-flip-energy convergence.','direct_placeholder_scan':placeholder,'local_compile_status':'NOT_PORTED_OR_COMPILED_BY_THIS_PREREAD'},'actual_apis':api,'route_at_most_seven_steps':[
 '1. Invoke the actual35 producer internally and destructure laws, everyN exact map identity, N0 dirac0, successor Tendsto to gaussianReal0,1. Freeze this SAME S_N and count normalization; do not replace with generic supplied weak-law premises.',
 '2. Derive continuity and genuine compact support of A_f,B_f,C_f: hf.continuous.pow2; Real.continuous_mul_log.comp; hf.continuous_deriv(1<=2); hs.comp_left with square-zero and tlogt-zero; hs.deriv and square-zero. No additional positivity or regularity premise.',
 '3. Use ROOT ofCompactSupport for each observer to obtain actual real BCFs. Derive their probability-law and gaussian L1 using Continuous.integrable_of_hasCompactSupport (or true bounded finite measure proof). Probability/finite-on-compacts are outputs/typeclass consequences, not premises on f.',
 '4. Apply ProbabilityMeasure.tendsto_iff_forall_integral_tendsto to actual35 Tendsto and each BCF. This produces limits for A_f, B_f and C_f on actual laws(n+1), including signed B_f and zeros.',
 '5. Prove actual S_N measurable via measurable_of_finite for canonical cube, rewrite lawsN via35 exact map, use integrable_map_measure and integral_map with observer actual continuity/strong measurability to output corresponding L1/integral identities under true mu_N. N0 identities remain dirac0, not variance1 approximation.',
 '6. Compose A_f integral convergence with Real.continuous_mul_log.continuousAt.tendsto; subtract from B_f convergence. Entropy limit is valid also when f=0 or integral f²=0; do not divide by mass or assume normalized f.',
 '7. Return same actual finite-law entropy and derivative-square observer limits for Bernoulli LSI consumer. Keep factor4 full-flip-energy MVT/exchangeability limit as a separate next parent, then only combine to compact1D Gaussian LSI after it is independently compiled.'
],'local_library_search':{'searched':'Samplinglib TechnicalLemmas Probability/FunctionalInequalities/Measure for actual entropy limits and bounded law-integral support before suggesting ports. No local actual count-law compact entropy producer found. Existing compact-gradient/L2 DCT and GaussianLipschitzExponential centered-exp DCT are different analytic contracts.','minimal_reuse':'Mathlib BCF constructor and weak-integral iff avoid importing any SLT limit implementation. Public34 Bernoulli may supply true mu_N probability/L1 for actual h=f(S_N); public35 supplies true weak law/map. If chosen, both are explicit dependency edges, not new source binders.','what_is_not_claimed':'No exhaustive theorem inventory/compiled36/localport or review of current35 implementation.'},'typed_first_residual':{'class':'dependency-ready-actual-integration-adapter','residual':'Implement and independently admit actual compact observer construction + allN L1 map/normalization transport and entropy limit against the sealed35 law output. API declarations exist pinned; no compiler/proofsearch conducted here, so elaboration/typeclass details remain untested.','counterexample_to_weak_L1_jump':'General weak probability convergence plus individual L1 is insufficient for noncompact unbounded observers: mu_n=(1-1/n)dirac0+(1/n)dirac n tends weakly dirac0, but integral x²=n. Thus actual source noncompact f cannot silently replace compact f at this node.'},'source_gap':['This is an authored C_c² core, not full Gaussian LSI on literal noncompact source f=sqrt(dR_y/dgamma).','Cutoff/density extension preserving entropy and Gaussian W1,2 energy, finite-Hilbert/product-domain extension and true Fisher-quarter adapter remain necessary.','Full flip-energy4 limit is independent; derivative observer convergence does not imply it.','Talagrand T2, full first4.6 W2, bias/fullLemma/main/work/composition remain open.'],'cost_boundary':'Bounded observer integral convergence gives no transport of arbitrary unbounded algorithm query cost, no numerical runtime/oracle complexity and no TV-to-cost inference.','reuse_earlier_closed_preread':{'path':(P/'source-detail-packet.json').as_posix(),'raw_sha256':desc(P/'source-detail-packet.json')['raw_sha256'],'scope':'Primary anchors/CLT retrieval and explicit separate factor4 route only. No previous source acceptance or decoder used to validate36 proof.'},'input_artifacts':inputs,'exposure':{'current35_body_read':False,'current35_blind_or_source_verdict_read':False,'root_future_candidate_or_prototype_read':False,'compiler_started':False,'proof_search_or_port_started':False,'newclaim_or_lifecycle_transition':False,'canonical_mutations':[]},'leases':{'read':'CLOSED','write':'CLOSED','compiler':'NOT_STARTED_CLOSED','Python':'CLOSED'}}
assert Path('lean-toolchain').read_text().strip()=='leanprover/lean4:v4.33.0'
